{
  "id": "25364_mohousuru",
  "headword": "{模倣|もほう}する",
  "reading": "もほうする",
  "romaji": "mohousuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "to imitate; to mimic; to copy",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to imitate; to mimic; to copy",
      "explanation": "To reproduce or closely follow the style, manner, or actions of someone or something, often with the aim of replicating it."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "25364_mohousuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{先生|せんせい}の{技|わざ}を{模倣|もほう}する。",
      "english": "To imitate the teacher's technique.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25364_mohousuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{子|こ}どもは{大人|おとな}の{行動|こうどう}を{模倣|もほう}して{学|まな}ぶ。",
      "english": "Children learn by imitating adults' behavior.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25364_mohousuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{他社|たしゃ}の{成功|せいこう}モデルを{模倣|もほう}するだけでは、{長期的|ちょうきてき}な{成長|せいちょう}は{難|むずか}しい。",
      "english": "Just imitating another company's success model won't lead to long-term growth.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "25364_mohousuru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{有名|ゆうめい}ブランドの{模倣品|もほうひん}が{市場|しじょう}に{出回|でまわ}っている。",
      "english": "Counterfeit goods imitating famous brands are circulating in the market.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal, somewhat academic word. Can be neutral (learning through imitation) or negative (unauthorized copying). In academic and artistic contexts, it's a standard term for discussing how works or behaviors are replicated.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {模倣品|もほうひん}: imitation product; counterfeit\n- {模倣|もほう}{犯罪|はんざい}: copycat crime\n- {模倣|もほう}{行為|こうい}: act of imitation\n- {自然|しぜん}を{模倣|もほう}する: to imitate nature\n- {模倣|もほう}から{創造|そうぞう}へ: from imitation to creation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {真似|まね}する: to imitate, to copy — everyday word; can be playful or critical\n- {物真似|ものまね}: impersonation — specifically imitating a person for entertainment\n- {模写|もしゃ}する: to copy (artwork) — specifically reproducing visual art\n- {偽造|ぎぞう}する: to forge, to counterfeit — criminal connotation, creating fakes with intent to deceive",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
